    "narrative": "For the Zurich Zebras, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) stands as the clear cornerstone of today\u2019s lineup. Facing the hittable Junk, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite combination of a favorable SP_xERA (4.67) and a premium leadoff spot. His projection is bolstered by a massive +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a strong .377 xwOBA, making him the only \"Elite\" tier play on our roster today. Conversely, the matchups for **Yordan Alvarez** (57.60) and **Junior Caminero** (58.05) remain tricky as they draw tough assignments against Gilbert and Fried, respectively; however, the high-floor profile of **Trea Turner** (65.99) remains a reliable anchor in the #2 hole despite facing a respectable arm in May.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest decision centered on the outfield and utility spots, ultimately sidelining potential depth in favor of maximizing efficiency. While **Caleb Durbin** (48.58) and **Carson Benge** (47.17) narrowly earned the nod, both are drifting toward our \"Marginal\" threshold due to unfavorable platoon splits\u2014specifically **Carson Benge** facing a challenging L/L matchup against Gore. We are exercising extreme caution with **Christian Yelich** (53.14); while his platoon edge against Wheeler is helpful, the underlying SP skill of the opposing pitcher makes this a high-risk start. We have effectively cleared the deck of non-starters, with **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** sidelined by rainouts, and **Colt Keith** remaining unavailable on the IL. With **Gary Sanchez** also confirmed out of the lineup, our focus remains strictly on the active efficiency of our core group.",
